What:           /sys/class/sec/tsp/dt2w_timeout
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        HTML6405
Description:
                Maximum double-tap-to-wake window in seconds after display
                powerdown. Accepts decimal values from 0 through 86400.
                The default is 300 (five minutes); 0 means unlimited. Changes apply
                on the next display powerdown and do not restart an active
                window. dt2w_enable must also be enabled.

                For example, 300 allows double-tap wake for five minutes.
                At expiry, the driver restores the saved touch configuration,
                disables the touch IRQ, powers off the controller and releases
                its suspend blocker. Full system suspend is then permitted;
                other wake locks may still prevent it. Use the power button
                or another supported wake source after expiry. Display resume
                powers the controller back on; the next display powerdown
                starts a new window.

                On this board the touch interrupt uses a normal GPIO, so
                full system suspend is blocked while gesture wake is active.
                This setting does not make that interrupt wake-capable.
